Myth: The cycle of light had stuttered once more. Avaris stood at the edge of the chasm, his hands open, waiting for the golden seeds that should have materialized from the mist. Instead, only the cold, biting wind of the Void greeted his palms. The silence was absolute, a stark reminder that even the most determined architect cannot bridge the divide alone. He had cast his own offering into the dark, hoping to spark a return, yet the other side remained shrouded in a stubborn, impenetrable hesitation. The bridge, which he had labored to reconstruct with such hope, trembled under the weight of the missing harvest.

He realized that the architecture of trust was fragile, easily dismantled by the refusal to participate. The mist seemed to thicken, mocking his attempt to revive the resonance that once defined their covenant. He stood firm, not in anger, but in the sad clarity of the architect whose designs are ignored. Without the sender’s contribution, the prism remained dark, unlit by the trade that transforms scarcity into abundance. Avaris watched the empty space between them, understanding that while he could offer the architecture of faith, he could not force the hand of his counterpart to build the bridge.

